{
  "matches": [
    {
      "refs": [
        "init:i1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To begin the process, Rental Items are Returned to the Store."
      ],
      "justification": "Structural init node implicitly supported by the opening clause signaling process start."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->c2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Customer returns the items to the store,\" then we can continue the process. However, if the \"Delivery Crew picks-up items at the event site,\" then we also continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Branch node and guards faithfully capture the two conditional alternatives; converge node implicitly supported by the rejoined flow after continuation."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "During this step, the items are counted and compared to the original contract."
      ],
      "justification": "Action content directly paraphrases the counting/comparison instruction without altering granularity or qualifiers."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n5",
        "guard:b2->n6",
        "guard:b2->n9",
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Order is complete and all items were returned,\" then we proceed with the process. However, if the \"Order is incomplete and items are missing,\" we still continue the process. Similarly, if the \"Order is complete but items are damaged,\" we email the customer to inform them of the damage and additional charges."
      ],
      "justification": "Branch, guards, and the email action accurately reflect the three-order-status split and the damage notification step; converge node marks the implicit path rejoin."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b3->c3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After this, if the \"Items are packed for an existing order,\" we continue the process. Alternatively, if the \"Items are stored for future orders,\" we also continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Branch and guards exactly mirror the pack-vs-store decision; converge node supported by subsequent process continuation."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "In case of missing items and replacement charges, we email the customer to inform them."
      ],
      "justification": "Action faithfully restates the missing-item email instruction."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Additionally, if there are damaged items and additional charges, we temporarily take them out of inventory."
      ],
      "justification": "Action precisely captures the temporary inventory removal step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n7",
        "guard:b4->c4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Customer returns the missing items,\" we continue the process. However, if the \"Customer does not return the missing items,\" we still continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Branch, guards, and action (modeling the condition as a step per allowed convention) fully cover the return/no-return decision and rejoin."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Finally, when the process is complete, it ends."
      ],
      "justification": "End node and redundant action step both faithfully reflect the stated process termination."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n11",
        "action:n12",
        "action:n13",
        "guard:b5->n12",
        "guard:b5->n13"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the \"Items are repaired and added into inventory,\" we continue the process. On the other hand, if the \"Items can't be repaired and are discarded,\" we email the customer with replacement charges."
      ],
      "justification": "Branch, guards, and action steps accurately implement the repair/discard decision and associated outcomes."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b6->c5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Lastly, the items are packed for an existing order. If the \"Items are packed for an existing order,\" we continue the process. If the \"Items are stored for future orders,\" we also continue the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Branch and guards correctly model the second pack/store routing decision; converge marks path rejoin."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n15"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once again, when the process is complete, it ends."
      ],
      "justification": "Structural end and action step match the explicit termination statement."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n16"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once again, when the process is complete, it ends."
      ],
      "justification": "End node and action align with the final completion statement."
    }
  ],
